  "notes": "Paper presents projected sensitivity to vector B-L (and B) dark photon dark matter using an optomechanical accelerometer (SiN membrane + Be mirror). The main result is a projection on the g_B-L coupling vs mass plane (Fig. 2), spanning roughly mDM ~ 1e-12 to 1e-10 eV with sensitivities below g~1e-22. No numerical table is provided; data only appears as plotted curves, so no reliable (mass, coupling) pairs could be extracted. This is a projection, not a measured limit. Local DM density 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed. | Vision: Figure 2 shows projected sensitivity (blue/green curves) and existing constraints (pink Eot-Wash, red LIGO, blue MICROSCOPE). The lower boundary of the excluded region is traced: dominated by LIGO/MICROSCOPE at low mass (rising sensitivity ~1e-20 down to ~7e-23) and Eot-Wash flat at ~7e-23 to 1e-22 in mid range, rising at high mass. Coupling type is VectorBL (g_BL). Axis calibration per provided ranges. | Calibration: Spot-check calibration: verify/stage2 ratio=2.1x",
